        <h2>Chapter 15 — Accountability &amp; Discipline</h2>
        <span class="urdu-section-title urdu-text" dir="rtl">باب پانزدہم — ہمہ وقتی احتساب، غفلت اور تادیبی کارروائی</span>

        <p>Every office holder is fully answerable for their position, fund stewardship, and conduct. If any member misuses public funds, exceeds constitutional powers, or fails to perform assigned duties:</p>

        <ul class="styled-doc-list">
          <li>A formal written show-cause notice is served allowing 7 days to present an oral and written defense.</li>
          <li>An impartial 3-member inquiry commission is formed by the Executive Committee.</li>
          <li>Upon finding of culpability, the Executive Committee or General Body may reprimand, suspend, or vote for immediate disqualification.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- Chapter 16 -->
      <section id="ch16" class="doc-section card reveal-on-scroll">
        <div class="section-meta-header">
          <span class="article-badge">Democratic Decorum &bull; اختلافِ رائے</span>
          <span class="chapter-index-chip">Chapter 16</span>
        </div>
        <h2>Chapter 16 — Difference of Opinion</h2>
        <span class="urdu-section-title urdu-text" dir="rtl">باب شانزدہم — اختلافِ رائے کا احترام اور اکثریتی فیصلے کی پابندی</span>

        <p>
          Constructive difference of opinion is embraced as a catalyst for institutional vitality. Every member holds the inviolable right to voice dissent during debates. 
          However, once a matter has been decided through constitutional voting, <strong>all members are bound to respect and execute the final consensus</strong> with undivided loyalty.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Chapter 17 -->
      <section id="ch17" class="doc-section card reveal-on-scroll">
        <div class="section-meta-header">
          <span class="article-badge">Tenure Limits &bull; مدتِ نظامت</span>
          <span class="chapter-index-chip">Chapter 17</span>
        </div>
        <h2>Chapter 17 — Term of Office &amp; Handover</h2>
        <span class="urdu-section-title urdu-text" dir="rtl">باب ہفدہم — مدتِ نظامت (۲ سال) اور تمام ریکارڈ کی منتقلی</span>

        <p>
          To prevent entrenchment and dynastic control, the tenure of all Executive Committee office holders is strictly capped at <strong>two (2) years</strong>.
        </p>

        <div class="handover-checklist card p-4 mt-3">
          <h4>Mandatory Handover Protocol at Term Completion:</h4>
          <ol class="styled-numbered-list">
            <li>Comprehensive presentation of the 24-month audit and administrative completion ledger before the General Body.</li>
            <li>Democratic elections or consensus nominations supervised by the Advisory Council.</li>
            <li>Formal physical handing over of all official bank checkbooks, ledger books, resolution archives, and seal stamps within 14 days.</li>
          </ol>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Chapter 18 -->
      <section id="ch18" class="doc-section card reveal-on-scroll">
        <div class="section-meta-header">
          <span class="article-badge">Constitutional Law &bull; آئینی ترامیم</span>
          <span class="chapter-index-chip">Chapter 18</span>
        </div>
        <h2>Chapter 18 — Constitutional Amendments</h2>
        <span class="urdu-section-title urdu-text" dir="rtl">باب ہجدہم — آئین میں ترامیم کا ۵ مرحلہ وار طریقہ کار</span>

        <p>
          No article of this Constitution may be altered, modified, or diluted at the subjective whim of any single person or faction. 
          Any amendment must undergo this rigorous 5-step procedure:
        </p>

        <div class="amendment-steps-grid">
          <div class="amend-step"><span class="amend-num">1</span><strong>Written Motion</strong><p>Formal proposal sponsored by at least 5 council members.</p></div>
          <div class="amend-step"><span class="amend-num">2</span><strong>Council Debate</strong><p>Full clause-by-clause reading in regular session.</p></div>
          <div class="amend-step"><span class="amend-num">3</span><strong>Legal Review</strong><p>Vetting by Legal Advisors and Ulama Council.</p></div>
          <div class="amend-step"><span class="amend-num">4</span><strong>Two-Thirds Majority</strong><p>Ratification by $\ge 66.7\%$ vote of the General Body.</p></div>
          <div class="amend-step"><span class="amend-num">5</span><strong>Gazette Entry</strong><p>Permanent codification into the official register.</p></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Part 2: Operational Policy Manual -->
      <section id="policy" class="doc-section card card-gold-accent reveal-on-scroll">
        <div class="section-meta-header">
          <span class="article-badge text-gold">Part 2 &bull; تنظیمی پالیسی و رہنما اصول</span>
          <span class="chapter-index-chip">Operational Manual</span>
        </div>
        <h2>Part 2: Operational Policy Manual</h2>
        <span class="urdu-section-title urdu-text" dir="rtl">حصہ دوم: توغ امن کمیٹی کے ۱۸ عملی ضوابط اور نافذ العمل اصول</span>

        <p class="lead-text">
          Approved alongside the 18 chapters to regulate administrative dispatch, privacy protection, emergency protocols, and institutional discipline:
        </p>

        <div class="policy-table-wrapper">
          <table class="policy-table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>No.</th>
                <th>Policy Rule</th>
                <th>Operational Mandate</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td><strong>1</strong></td>
                <td><strong>Principle of Written Resolution</strong></td>
                <td>Verbal orders carry zero legal authority. Every binding decision requires an approved resolution.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><strong>2</strong></td>
                <td><strong>Meeting Convening Protocol</strong></td>
                <td>Sessions called by General Secretary with written notice and distributed agenda.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><strong>3</strong></td>
                <td><strong>Agenda &amp; Written Minutes</strong></td>
                <td>Mandatory MoM recording decisions, responsible officers, and target dates.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><strong>4</strong></td>
                <td><strong>Collective Decision-Making</strong></td>
                <td>Solo decrees strictly prohibited; all matters determined via consultation and majority vote.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><strong>5</strong></td>
                <td><strong>Total Financial Transparency</strong></td>
                <td>Safe double-entry bookkeeping, receipts, vouchers, and cash reconciliation.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><strong>6</strong></td>
                <td><strong>Donation Receipt Guarantee</strong></td>
                <td>Numbered receipt issued for every cash or online contribution.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><strong>7</strong></td>
                <td><strong>Fund Disbursement Thresholds</strong></td>
                <td>Prior council approval required for expenditures exceeding minor discretionary petty limits.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><strong>8</strong></td>
                <td><strong>Periodic Financial Reports</strong></td>
                <td>Quarterly balance sheets posted publicly for community scrutiny.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><strong>9</strong></td>
                <td><strong>Project Lead &amp; Deadlines</strong></td>
                <td>Every initiative assigned to a named officer with enforceable milestone deadlines.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><strong>10</strong></td>
                <td><strong>Quarterly Progress Audits</strong></td>
                <td>Monitoring completed, ongoing, and delayed milestones systematically.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><strong>11</strong></td>
                <td><strong>Conflict of Interest Avoidance</strong></td>
                <td>Mandatory recusal from decisions touching personal, family, or business interests.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><strong>12</strong></td>
                <td><strong>Verified Fact-Checking</strong></td>
                <td>Documentary evidence required before formulating petitions against any department or official.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><strong>13</strong></td>
                <td><strong>Audited Grievance Pipeline</strong></td>
                <td>Central Complaint Register logging intake, department routing, and citizen resolution.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><strong>14</strong></td>
                <td><strong>Whistleblower Privacy Protection</strong></td>
                <td>Redaction of sensitive PII to safeguard reporting citizens from harassment.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><strong>15</strong></td>
                <td><strong>Lawful Institutional Collaboration</strong></td>
                <td>Cooperation with police and district administration without replacing state authority.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><strong>16</strong></td>
                <td><strong>Ban on Self-Help / Vigilantism</strong></td>
                <td>Absolute prohibition of coercion, threats, force, or unauthorized physical action.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><strong>17</strong></td>
                <td><strong>Strict Political Neutrality</strong></td>
                <td>No party banners, no campaign funding, and equal respect for all residents.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><strong>18</strong></td>
                <td><strong>Public Trust Principle</strong></td>
                <td>Positions are solemn responsibilities before Allah and the public, not sources of personal power.</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </section>

